Subject: [URGENT QUALITY ALERT] OOS Residual Solvent & Yield Deficit - Azithromycin Dihydrate (Batch AZM-2603-09)
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 08:15:30 +0000

QUALITY INCIDENT ALERT: DEV-2026-0610

Attention QA Investigation Team,

Batch AZM-2603-09 of Azithromycin Dihydrate API (Batch size: 200 kg nominal, RCVD-102 Vacuum Cone Dryer) has generated an Out-of-Specification (OOS) analytical result upon completion of the 24-hour drying cycle:

1. Out-of-Specification Result:
   - Residual Solvent (Acetone by GC Headspace): 7,200 ppm (ICH Q3C Limit: Not More Than 5,000 ppm)
   - Actual isolated yield: 142.3 kg (Historical average: 174.0 kg, -18.2% yield loss)
   - Water Content (KF): 4.8% (Conforming to dihydrate stoichiometry)

2. Critical Process Parameter Deviation:
   - Vacuum trend logs from VCD-102 indicate chamber pressure degraded from 15 mbar to 280 mbar between hour 6 and hour 14 of the drying cycle.
   - Liquid nitrogen cold trap condenser temperature rose to +8°C due to an intermittent cryogenic solenoid valve blockage.

3. Engineering Preliminary Teardown:
   - Maintenance inspected dry vacuum pump VP-102 and found a fractured graphite mechanical shaft seal ring, permitting atmospheric nitrogen and air ingress into the vacuum manifold.
   - The reduced vacuum impaired acetone sublimation kinetics, preventing desorption from the dihydrate crystal interstices.

Immediate Actions Taken:
- Batch AZM-2603-09 tagged with QA Red Hold Tag #HLD-9982.
- RCVD-102 placed out of service.
- Work order WO-ENG-2026-7788 issued for vacuum pump replacement.

Please initiate full Root Cause Analysis (Fishbone, 5 Whys, CAPA).

